  "notes": "Williams System 6 diagnostics per the Blackout instruction booklet 16P-495-103, Diagnostic Procedures steps 1-5: with the Auto-Up/Manual-Down toggle (public -6) at Manual-Down, Advance (public -7) blanks the displays; Advance plus Auto-Up runs the display-digits test; Advance runs Test 01 (lamps); Manual-Down plus Advance enters Test 02 and pulses solenoid 01, and each further Advance pulses the next solenoid while the ball-in-play display shows its number. Twenty-three further Advances run past the last step to show where the test wraps. Direct switch writes only; public -6 reads 1 for Auto-Up. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
